// The clerk's split of what the owner typed (plan/edge.md S3, paper-research m709-m711). A filing's step `file` is
// owed by clerk, which coordd answers itself: it runs `place` below once, statelessly, finds each passage in the
// owner's text (a passage that is not the owner's words as typed is refused) and answers `file` (file.call) with
// their spans, or Unplaced with what could not be placed. The owner's text is never copied: a piece is a span of it.
// OPEN is coordd's: each open ticket, one a line, with its kind, title, and the step it owes the owner if it does.

type Passage {
  ticket: Ticket
  passage: Text
  answer: Text?
}

call place(text: Text, open: Text) -> Placed(pieces: [Passage], rest: Text?)
  task clerk
  template
    You are the clerk of a software team. The owner typed the message below. Each part of it is meant for one of the
    open tickets listed after it. Split the message into passages, each a stretch of the owner's words copied exactly
    as typed (same spelling, case, punctuation; never rephrase, fix or shorten them), and say which ticket each is for.

    A passage that answers a step the ticket owes the owner gets that step's result as its answer, but only when the
    words leave exactly one of the results listed for it (for "Yes | No", "go ahead" is Yes, "not now" is No); when
    they could mean more than one, or none, give no answer, and the passage is a post on the ticket.

    Keep the passages in the order the owner wrote them, and leave no word out: a joining word between two passages
    ("and", "also", "then") belongs to the passage it starts. Anything that belongs to no open ticket goes in rest,
    copied exactly; leave rest empty when all of it is placed.

    The message:
    <<<
    {{ text }}
    >>>

    The open tickets:
    {{ open }}
